  <Widget no="2" caption="check yourself: the three calculations managers actually get wrong" widget="quiz" config={corpfinQuiz} />
  <p>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> these are the three calculations managers actually get
    wrong. Question 1 tempts you to forget the tax shield on interest — the single most common
    exam error, and the difference between a right and wrong hurdle rate. Question 2 tests
    whether the irrelevance theorem has really landed: if debt looked "cheaper" to you, reread
    Proposition II before touching a balance sheet. Question 3 prices trade credit the way the
    working-capital section taught — annualise the implied rate before accepting "free" terms.
  </p>
